course: dictionary
lesson: 13218
title: Futile: when trying cannot work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Futile means that something has no chance of working. However hard you try, nothing you do can change the result. Trying is a waste of effort.
explain: «It was futile to run, because the bus had already left.» Running cannot make a bus wait. The word tells you the effort could never succeed.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Phrases like «no chance», «a waste», «still failed» or «could not change anything» often point to futile.
fact: Futile is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as an attempt, an effort or a struggle.
fact: «Futile» means having no chance of success; useless.
fact: Useful phrases: «a futile attempt», «a futile effort», «it is futile to».
fact: In stories, a futile struggle shows that a character feels hopeless.
fact: People may argue about whether something is futile or whether it is still worth trying.
exercise: «Shouting at the wind was futile; it just kept blowing.» What does futile mean? | Loud and angry | Very windy and fun | *Having no chance of success | Quick and easy
exercise: Which phrase describes a try that cannot work? | a sunny afternoon | a warm drink | *a futile attempt | a loud cheer
exercise: Ella says, «It is futile to shout at the closed door. Nobody can hear me.» Why is shouting futile here? | It makes the door open | It is very loud and fun | It is quiet and calm | *It cannot change anything, because nobody can hear
test: «The team's futile effort ended in defeat.» What does futile suggest? | *Useless, with no chance of winning | Very fast | Long and tiring | Cheerful and fun
test: Which word is closest in meaning to futile? | Lucky | *Pointless | Bright | Helpful
exam: Why is it futile to run after a bus that has already left? | Because the bus will stop for you | Because buses are slow | Because running is fun | *Because running cannot change the bus leaving
